{"id":"neet-2025-q085","pn":85,"y":"NEET 2025","tp":"Thermodynamics (Chemistry)","st":"Enthalpy of formation, Hess's law","q":"The standard heat of formation, in kcal/mol of Ba²⁺ is :\n[Given : standard heat of formation of SO₄²⁻ ion (aq) = –216 kcal/mol, standard heat of crystallisation of BaSO₄(s) = –4.5 kcal/mol, standard heat of formation of BaSO₄(s) = – 349 kcal/mol]","o":["– 128.5","– 133.0","+ 133.0","+ 220.5"],"c":0,"s":"(1) S + 2O₂ + 2e⁻ → SO₄²⁻, ΔH_f = –216 kcal/mol\n(2) Ba²⁺(g) + SO₄²⁻(g) → BaSO₄(s), ΔH_crystallisation = –4.5 kcal/mol\n(3) Ba + S + 2O₂ → BaSO₄(s), ΔH_f(BaSO₄) = –349 kcal/mol\n(4) Ba(s) → Ba²⁺(g) + 2e⁻\nEquation (4) is obtained from (1), (2) and (3) by applying (3) – (1) – (2).\nSo, –349 – (–4.5) – (–216)\n= –349 + 4.5 + 216\n= –349 + 220.5\n= –128.5 kcal/mol"}
